      "id": "librispeech-test.other-000035",
      "raw_transcript": "The grand dame whom he supplied with faggots, the merchant whom he rescued from robbers, the king's counselor to whom he gave aid, all became his friends. Up and down the land, to beggar or lord, homeless wanderer or high born dame, he gladly gave unselfish service all unsought, and such as he helped straight away became his friends.",
